<title>USA: KOCH OIL raises U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts. [CORRECTED 23:30 GMT]</title>
<headline>KOCH OIL raises U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts. [CORRECTED 23:30 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koch Oil said it raised the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents, effective Thursday (corrects from Friday).</p>
<p>The increase brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $20.25 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $17.75 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $20.00 and Oklahoma sweet is $20.50.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
